s head) or 'out' (its tail).","enum":["in","out"],"type":"string"},"lengthTicks":{"description":"Fade length in ticks, 0 or more; 0 removes the fade. The fade may not be longer than the clip \u2014 a trim or split that would leave it hanging over the edge is refused instead.","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"shape":{"description":"Fade curve: 'linear', 'equalPower', 'exponential' or 'logarithmic'. equalPower holds perceived loudness roughly constant and is the usual choice where two clips meet.","enum":["linear","equalPower","exponential","logarithmic"],"type":"string"}},"required":["clipId","edge","lengthTicks","shape"],"type":"object"},"clip.move":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"clipId":{"description":"Id of the clip to move.","minLength":1,"type":"string"},"startTicks":{"description":"New clip start, in absolute timeline ticks from 0 (PPQ 960: 960 ticks is a quarter note, 3840 is one 4/4 bar). The destination must be clear \u2014 clips on one track may not overlap.","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"trackId":{"description":"Destination track; equal to the clip's current track for a same-lane move.","minLength":1,"type":"string"}},"required":["clipId","trackId","startTicks"],"type":"object"},"clip.mute":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"clipId":{"description":"Id of the clip to mute or unmute.","minLength":1,"type":"string"},"muted":{"description":"true silences just this clip, false unmutes it. Absolute, not a toggle, and independent of track.mute.","type":"boolean"}},"required":["clipId","muted"],"type":"object"},"clip.phaseAnchor.set":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"anchorTicks":{"description":"Where this clip's warped source considers the bar grid to begin, in ticks, 0 or more. 0 is the unshifted default.","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"clipId":{"description":"Id of the clip whose bar-grid phase anchor changes.","minLength":1,"type":"string"}},"required":["clipId","anchorTicks"],"type":"object"},"clip.place":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"assetHash":{"description":"blake3 hash of the audio asset under audio/: 64 lowercase hex characters. The asset must already be in the package \u2014 this command references, it does not import.","pattern":"^[0-9a-f]{64}$","type":"string"},"clipId":{"description":"Caller-minted, stable id for the new clip; the engine never mints one. Must not already be in use anywhere in the project.","minLength":1,"type":"string"},"lengthTicks":{"description":"How long the clip is, in ticks. The schema admits 0 for historical reasons but the executor REFUSES it: this must be greater than 0.","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"sourceOffsetTicks":{"default":0,"description":"Optional offset INTO the asset at which the clip starts reading, in ticks. Default 0 (play from the top of the file). offset + length must stay inside the asset's extent.","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"startTicks":{"description":"Where the clip starts on the timeline, in absolute timeline ticks from 0 (PPQ 960: 960 ticks is a quarter note, 3840 is one 4/4 bar).","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"trackId":{"description":"Id of the track to place the clip on. Clips on one track may NOT overlap \u2014 an overlapping placement is refused, not nudged.","minLength":1,"type":"string"}},"required":["clipId","trackId","assetHash","startTicks","lengthTicks"],"type":"object"},"clip.placeMidi":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"clipId":{"description":"Caller-minted, stable id for the new note clip; the engine never mints one. Must not already be in use anywhere in the project.","minLength":1,"type":"string"},"lengthTicks":{"description":"How long the clip is, in ticks; must be greater than 0. Note positions are CLIP-RELATIVE, so this is the window they live in.","exclusiveMinimum":0,"type":"integer"},"startTicks":{"description":"Where the clip starts on the timeline, in absolute timeline ticks from 0 (PPQ 960: 960 ticks is a quarter note, 3840 is one 4/4 bar).","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"trackId":{"description":"Id of the track to place the clip on. Clips on one track may NOT overlap \u2014 an overlapping placement is refused.","minLength":1,"type":"string"}},"required":["clipId","trackId","startTicks","lengthTicks"],"type":"object"},"clip.remove":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"clipId":{"description":"Id of the clip to remove from the timeline. The underlying audio asset under audio/ is NOT deleted: it is content-addressed and other clips may reference it.","minLength":1,"type":"string"}},"required":["clipId"],"type":"object"},"clip.rename":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"clipId":{"description":"Id of the clip to relabel. Its id does not change \u2014 only the label a person sees.","minLength":1,"type":"string"},"name":{"description":"New display label for the clip. Non-empty.","minLength":1,"type":"string"}},"required":["clipId","name"],"type":"object"},"clip.setGain":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"clipId":{"description":"Id of the clip whose trim changes.","minLength":1,"type":"string"},"gainDb":{"description":"Clip gain trim in dB, -60 to 12; 0 is unity. Applied ON TOP OF the track fader (mix.gain), not instead of it. The bound is enforced by the executor, not only by this schema.","maximum":12,"minimum":-60,"type":"number"}},"required":["clipId","gainDb"],"type":"object"},"clip.split":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"atTicks":{"description":"Split point, in absolute timeline ticks from 0 (PPQ 960: 960 ticks is a quarter note, 3840 is one 4/4 bar), STRICTLY inside the clip: after its start and before its end. A split exactly on an edge is refused rather than silently ignored.","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"clipId":{"description":"Id of the clip to split. It becomes the LEFT piece and keeps this id; the right piece gets newClipId.","minLength":1,"type":"string"},"newClipId":{"description":"Caller-minted id for the RIGHT-hand piece the split creates; must not already be in use. The left piece keeps the original clipId.","minLength":1,"type":"string"}},"required":["clipId","atTicks","newClipId"],"type":"object"},"clip.trim":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"clipId":{"description":"Id of the clip to trim.","minLength":1,"type":"string"},"deltaTicks":{"description":"Signed tick delta, and it may not be 0. On the 'start' edge a positive value shortens from the front (the start moves later); on the 'end' edge a positive value lengthens. The result must leave a length greater than 0 and must not collide with a neighbouring clip.","type":"integer"},"edge":{"description":"Which edge moves: 'start' or 'end'. 'start' is REFUSED on a note-backed clip (it would shift every note relative to the clip); 'end' works on audio and note clips alike.","enum":["start","end"],"type":"string"}},"required":["clipId","edge","deltaTicks"],"type":"object"},"clip.warp.set":{"additionalProperties":false,"if":{"properties":{"mode":{"const":"ratio"}}},"properties":{"clipId":{"description":"Id of the clip whose time-warp changes.","minLength":1,"type":"string"},"mode":{"description":"'ratio' applies the fixed stretchRatio you supply and is the mode that does something. 'conform' is accepted and journaled, but this build resolves it to whatever stretchRatio the clip already carried: conform-to-project-tempo needs a stored SOURCE tempo the engine does not have yet (E7 warp markers), so it is not a tempo match today.","enum":["ratio","conform"],"type":"string"},"stretchRatio":{"description":"Playback stretch factor, greater than 0; 1.0 is unwarped and 2.0 plays at half speed. Optional at the top level of this schema but REQUIRED when mode is 'ratio' (the if/then branch pins it), and meaningless when mode is 'conform'. The renderer clamps what it can actually stretch to 0.25x..4x.","exclusiveMinimum":0,"type":"number"}},"required":["clipId","mode"],"then":{"required":["clipId","mode","stretchRatio"]},"type":"object"},"device.add":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"deviceId":{